"file editor" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		FileEditor
		<header>A CodeMirror editor on one Spell file at a time, kept in step with it.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>Where you type spell in the editor: a <link target="src-packages-app-docs-codemirroreditor-html" link="/code-mirror-editor">CodeMirrorEditor</> showing one file. What you type goes straight into the file, and a file loaded or reloaded shows in the editor.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone changing the spell app's editor, or reading its code</>
		<item icon="image">A picture, not live: it edits the editor's open file</>
	</>

	<section label="1. What it looks like">
		<icon slot="icon" name="image"/>
		<text paragraph>The editor's input pane, on the Solitaire example's cards: everything under the toolbar is a FileEditor on the open file.</>
		<image src="/components/app/_images/InputEditor.png" alt="The input pane: a File dropdown and actions above a code editor showing Card.spell, coloured as spell" appearance="bordered rounded"/>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>A picture, taken by <text code>yarn site:pictures</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>The <link target="src-packages-app-docs-inputeditor-html" link="/input-editor">InputEditor</> draws one, once CodeMirror has loaded, and shows each file in it:</>
		<text paragraph>InputEditor.tsx · the code pane's editor, shortened:</>
		<markdown>
			```typescript
			<Loading fallback={<LazyCodeMirror.Loading />}>
			  <LazyCodeMirror.FileEditor
			    file={file()}
			    hotkeys={EDITOR_HOTKEYS}
			    onMount={didMount}
			    onUpdate={editor.onInputUpdate}
			    onUnmount={editor.onInputWillUnmount}
			  />
			</Loading>
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>It shows the file's CodeMirror state, which the app's <text code>FileStates</> keep in step with the file both ways.</>
			<item>With no <text code>file</> yet, it says the editor's loading.</>
			<item>A new <text code>file</> shows in the same view, and the last one's state is kept: its undo, folds, selection and scroll, so switching back finds it as it was left. No remount per file.</>
			<item><text code>onMount</> hands out the editor, <text code>SpellCodeMirror</>, once it shows a file: the app follows its scrolling there, and its caret through <text code>onUpdate</>. Its keys are the page's, passed in as <text code>hotkeys</>.</>
			<item>Only the editor's pages need CodeMirror, so it's loaded after the program has compiled and run: draw it through <text code>LazyCodeMirror</>, inside a <text code>&lt;Loading&gt;</>, never by importing it.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Props, and where it's drawn">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="FileEditor"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its code, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

